# Web UX

When building or editing interactive surfaces (buttons, chips, sheets, dialogs, tabs, pickers, page/panel transitions):

- Apply engineering foundations and `code/web/ui` first (primitives, reuse, semantic elements).
- Load `skills/code/web/ux/SKILL.md` for behavior, motion, library choice, and generative sound.
- Load `references/library-selection.md` before adding animation or overlay dependencies.
- Load `references/shared/generative-sound.md` when wiring hover/click/dismiss audio (when repo adopts).
- Cancel and backdrop dismiss must run the full exit animation — no instant unmount.
- Reuse shared primitives from `code/web/ui` → `standard-primitives.md`.

Under `**/components/ui/**/mobile/**` or `**/desktop/**`, also follow **`mobile-ux.mdc`** / **`desktop-ux.mdc`** for viewport-specific references.

Key bar: transparent tap highlight, `focus-visible` rings, `:active`/`whileTap` feedback, portal overlays, generative sound when repo mandates, `prefers-reduced-motion`, check `package.json` before new deps.
